/**
 * @mainpage Constants Library
 *
 * @section intro Introduction
 *
 * This library provides a collection of commonly used mathematical
 * constants, unit-conversion macros, SI and IEC prefixes, and
 * data-type-related constants.
 *
 * The library is organized into three main categories:
 *
 * - Mathematical constants and precomputed values.
 * - Unit conversion and measurement prefixes.
 * - Data type limits, ranges, and floating-point precision values.
 *
 *
 * @section features Features
 *
 * The constants library provides:
 *
 * - Mathematical constants such as pi and tau.
 * - Precomputed powers of Euler's number.
 * - Precomputed square-root values.
 * - Precomputed cube-root values.
 * - Integer type minimum and maximum values.
 * - Floating-point range and magnitude constants.
 * - Floating-point machine epsilon values.
 * - Length, mass, and time conversions.
 * - Frequency and period conversions.
 * - Temperature conversions.
 * - Angle conversions.
 * - Rotational speed conversions.
 * - SI decimal prefixes.
 * - IEC binary prefixes.
 *
 *
 * @section headers Header Files
 *
 * The library is provided through the following headers:
 *
 * - @ref constants.h - Main header that includes all constant definitions.
 * - @ref constants_math.h - Mathematical constants and precomputed values.
 * - @ref constants_units.h - Unit conversion macros and SI/IEC prefixes.
 * - @ref constants_data_type.h - Data type range and precision constants.
 *
 *
 * @section math Mathematical Constants
 *
 * The mathematical constants header provides commonly used values of
 * pi, tau, Euler's number, square roots, and cube roots.
 *
 * Examples include:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double pi  = MATH_PI;
 * double tau = MATH_TAU;
 * double e   = MATH_e;
 *
 * double sqrt_2 = MATH_SQRT_2;
 * double cbrt_2 = MATH_CUBRT_2;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Precomputed multiples and sub-multiples of pi are also available,
 * together with powers of Euler's number and roots from 2 through 25.
 *
 *
 * @section units Unit Conversion
 *
 * The unit conversion header provides macros for commonly used
 * engineering and scientific unit conversions.
 *
 * @subsection length Length
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double meters = IN_2_M(10.0);
 * double feet   = M_2_FT(2.0);
 * double miles  = M_2_MILE(1609.344);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection mass Mass
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double kg = LB_2_KG(10.0);
 * double lb = KG_2_LB(5.0);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection time Time
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double ms = SEC_2_MS(2.0);
 * double s  = MS_2_SEC(500.0);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection frequency Frequency and Period
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double period = HZ_2_SEC(100.0);
 * double freq   = SEC_2_HZ(0.01);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection temperature Temperature
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double fahrenheit = C_2_F(25.0);
 * double kelvin     = C_2_K(25.0);
 * double celsius    = F_2_C(77.0);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection angle Angle
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double radians = DEG_2_RAD(90.0);
 * double degrees = RAD_2_DEG(MATH_PI);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection rotational_speed Rotational Speed
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double radps = RPM_2_RADPS(1000.0);
 * double rpm   = RADPS_2_RPM(10.0);
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section prefixes Prefixes
 *
 * The library provides SI decimal prefixes ranging from @c QUETTA
 * through @c QUECTO.
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double mega = MEGA;
 * double micro = MICRO;
 * double nano = NANO;
 * @endcode
 *
 * IEC binary prefixes are also provided:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * auto kibi = KIBI;
 * auto mebi = MEBI;
 * auto gibi = GIBI;
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section datatype Data Type Constants
 *
 * The data type constants header provides minimum and maximum values
 * for integer types together with floating-point range and precision
 * constants.
 *
 * Examples:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * auto int_min = INT_32_MIN;
 * auto int_max = INT_32_MAX;
 *
 * double epsilon = DOUBLE_EPSILON;
 * float  small   = FLOAT_SMALL;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Floating-point constants include:
 *
 * - @c FLOAT_MIN
 * - @c FLOAT_MAX
 * - @c FLOAT_MIN_POS
 * - @c FLOAT_SMALL
 * - @c FLOAT_BIG
 * - @c FLOAT_EPSILON
 * - @c DOUBLE_MIN
 * - @c DOUBLE_MAX
 * - @c DOUBLE_MIN_POS
 * - @c DOUBLE_SMALL
 * - @c DOUBLE_BIG
 * - @c DOUBLE_EPSILON
 *
 *
 * @section usage Basic Usage
 *
 * The complete constants library can be included through the main
 * header:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "constants.h"
 *
 * double angle = DEG_2_RAD(90.0);
 * double value = MATH_PI * 2.0;
 * double time  = MS_2_SEC(100.0);
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section organization Library Organization
 *
 * The library is divided into the following functional groups:
 *
 * - Mathematical constants:
 *   @c constants_math.h
 * - Unit conversions and prefixes:
 *   @c constants_units.h
 * - Data type constants:
 *   @c constants_data_type.h
 * - Unified library interface:
 *   @c constants.h
 *
 *
 * @section copyright Copyright
 *
 * Copyright (c) 2026 Abhinay Kumar
 */